142
00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:41.600
He was like, I don't even know.
他当时说：我甚至不知道。

143
00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:42.520
Do I have DMs?
我有私信功能吗？

144
00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.140
So, I'm like, yes.
所以我说：有的。

145
00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.940
But I found an old email and we got in touch and it was so fun to talk to him.
但我找到了一封旧邮件，我们取得了联系，和他聊天真是太有趣了。

146
00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:49.720
He's a huge fan of the podcaSt.
他是我们播客的忠实粉丝。

147
00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:57.580
Jenna, he told me that he listens to the podcast in the evenings and then sometimes when he drifts off to sleep, he dreams like that he's in the podcast with us.
珍娜，他告诉我他晚上会听我们的播客，有时在快睡着的时候，他会梦见自己和我们一起录播客。

148
00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:58.340
Oh, my goodness.
噢，天哪。

149
00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:00.780
Is that a good dream or a nightmare?
那是美梦还是噩梦？

150
00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:01.280
I don't know.
我不知道。

151
00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:02.440
I hope it's a good thing.
希望这是件好事。

152
00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:03.160
I hope so.
我也希望如此。

153
00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.420
Erin had lots of great stuff to share.
艾琳有很多精彩的内容要分享。

154
00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.020
We're going to hit him up quite a bit.
我们之后会经常找他请教。

155
00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.400
We have Erin now.
我们现在有艾琳了。

156
00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.020
We have James and also Randy Cordrick.
我们有詹姆斯，还有兰迪·科德里克。

157
00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.580
I'm like, yes, when Angela told me that she got a hold of Erin.
当安吉拉告诉我她联系上艾琳时，我心想，太棒了。

158
00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:18.300
I know you were going to ask him about the office, but I had an Everybody Loves Raymond question.
我知道你本来打算问他关于《办公室》的事，但我有个关于《人人都爱雷蒙德》的问题。

159
00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:19.680
Still, this poor man.
不过，这可怜人。

160
00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:24.980
I cornered him on set and now you're calling him on the phone and my question is still about Everybody Loves Raymond.
我在片场堵住他，现在你又打电话给他，而我的问题还是关于《人人都爱雷蒙德》的。

161
00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.060
But here's the thing.
但重点是。

162
00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:32.780
I remember that there was this episode that was based on a story from his real life, but I couldn't remember all the details.
我记得有一集是基于他真实生活中的故事改编的，但我记不清所有细节了。

163
00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:34.080
It's the episode.
就是那一集。

164
00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:36.120
It's called 10th Anniversary.
叫作《十周年纪念》。

165
00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:45.680
And Ray and Deborah are celebrating their 10th anniversary and they want to watch their wedding tape and they get it out and they put it in the VCR.
雷和黛博拉在庆祝结婚十周年，他们想看婚礼录像带，于是拿出来放进录像机里。

166
00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:51.880
They press play and Ray has recorded a football game over their wedding tape.
他们按下播放键，结果发现雷在他们的婚礼录像带上录了一场橄榄球比赛。

167
00:08:52.340 --> 00:09:00.040
And I remember that there is some story where I think Erin recorded over his wedding tape with his wife.
我记得有个故事，好像是艾琳在录制他和他妻子的婚礼录像带时，不小心覆盖了内容。

168
00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.460
That is true.
那是真的。

169
00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:02.600
I knew it.
我就知道。

170
00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.160
That is true.
那是真的。

171
00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:04.500
So this is what happened.
事情是这样的。

172
00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.440
Okay, so Erin was a fan of Everybody Loves Raymond.
好吧，艾琳当时是《人人都爱雷蒙德》的粉丝。

173
00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.120
It was a show he wanted to meet on.
那是他想去面试的剧。

174
00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:13.860
So he thought, oh, I'll record a few episodes, watch them, really study the show.
所以他想，哦，我要录几集，看看，好好研究一下这部剧。

175
00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.860
So when I go in and meet, you know, I have all this information.
这样我去面试的时候，我就能掌握所有信息了。

176
00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.240
So he popped in a VHS.
于是他塞进了一盘录像带。

177
00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:21.120
Guys, this dates us all a little bit.
伙计们，这暴露了我们的年龄。

178
00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:24.480
And he hit record and it was his wedding video.
他按下了录制键，结果那是他的婚礼录像。

179
00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:25.320
Yeah.
是啊。

180
00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.040
And back then, you guys, it's not like you have multiple copies.
那时候，伙计们，不像现在有那么多备份。

181
00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:30.600
Like you get your wedding videotape and that's it.
就像你拿到婚礼录像带，那就只有那一盘。

182
00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:30.960
Yeah.
是啊。

183
00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:31.780
Yeah.
是啊。

184
00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.140
His wife was really upset.
他妻子非常生气。

185
00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:33.920
Oh, no.
噢，不。

186
00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:38.280
And he went in to meet on Everybody Loves Raymond and he told that story.
他去面试《人人都爱雷蒙德》时讲了这个故事。

187
00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:42.740
He was like, I taped over my wedding video to watch Everybody Loves Raymond.
他说，我为了看《人人都爱雷蒙德》，把我的婚礼录像给覆盖了。

188
00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.780
So my wife is really mad.
所以我妻子非常生气。

189
00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:46.180
You got to give me this job.
你们一定要给我这份工作。

190
00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:47.600
And he got the job.
然后他得到了那份工作。

191
00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:50.500
And then that story made it into an episode.
后来那个故事被写进了一集剧本里。

192
00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:51.160
Yes.
没错。

193
00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:53.120
Oh, I love it.
噢，我太喜欢这个了。

194
00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:56.280
A lot of Aaron's life ends up in scripts, you guys.
艾琳生活中的很多事最终都进了剧本，伙计们。

195
00:09:56.620 --> 00:10:01.200
There's a few episodes coming up that his actual life inspired things that Michael does.
接下来的几集里，有一些情节就是受他真实生活的启发，是迈克尔做过的事。

196
00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:02.720
And I can't wait to share those with you.
我迫不及待想和你们分享这些了。

197
00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.520
I'm so glad we're in touch with him.
我真高兴我们和他保持着联系。

198
00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.120
I know.
我知道。

199
00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.980
Fast fact number two.
冷知识之二。

200
00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:11.180
Angela, we shot this episode in August of 2008.
安吉拉，我们是在2008年8月拍摄这一集的。

201
00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:11.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

202
00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:17.880
And since we brought it up before, I thought it was worth mentioning that this same month,
既然之前提到了，我觉得值得一提的是，就在同一个月，

203
00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:25.660
Steve Carell won his second surfboard at the 2008 Teen Choice Awards for TV Comedy Actor.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔在2008年青少年选择奖上凭借电视喜剧男演员奖赢得了他的第二块冲浪板。

204
00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:27.900
Steve, where did you put your surfboards?
史蒂夫，你把你的冲浪板放哪儿了？

205
00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:29.340
Back-to-pack surfboards.
背靠背的冲浪板。

206
00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:29.780
Wow.
哇哦。

207
00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:34.060
When we have him on the podcast, is it going to be weird if we ask him where his surfboards are?
等他上我们播客的时候，如果我们问他冲浪板在哪儿，会不会很奇怪？

208
00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:36.060
It depends where you put him.
那得看你把他放在哪儿了。

209
00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.460
It's going to be such a weird question.
这问题听起来会很奇怪。

210
00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:47.520
Well, also, this same year, the movie Juno won Best Comedy Movie and Rainn Wilson was in that.
嗯，还有，同一年，《朱诺》获得了最佳喜剧电影奖，雷恩·威尔森也参演了那部电影。

211
00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:48.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

212
00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:51.720
Also, this same year, we won a SAG Award.
另外，同一年，我们还赢得了演员工会奖。

213
00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:52.680
Yes.
没错。

214
00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:56.920
So this was like the awards and the surfboards were coming in now.
所以那时候就像是奖项和冲浪板接踵而至。

215
00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:57.440
Yeah.
是啊。

216
00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:57.840
Right?
对吧？

217
00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:58.880
It was really cool.
真的很酷。

218
00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:05.680
And I remember at the 2008 SAG Awards, we were sitting at the table, and everybody was like,
我记得在2008年的演员工会奖颁奖礼上，我们坐在桌旁，大家都在说，

219
00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:07.500
who's going to give the speech if we win?
如果我们赢了，谁去发表获奖感言？

220
00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:09.380
And we all assumed it would be Steve.
我们都以为会是史蒂夫。

221
00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:10.860
Like, Steve will give the speech.
就像是，史蒂夫会去发表感言。

222
00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:12.860
And Steve said, guys, this is an ensemble.
结果史蒂夫说，伙计们，这是一个集体奖。

223
00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.880
I don't want to always speak for the caSt.
我不想总是代表剧组发言。

224
00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.340
That doesn't feel right to me.
我觉得那样不太合适。

225
00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.000
This is an ensemble award.
这是个集体奖项。

226
00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.560
I think someone else should speak.
我觉得应该由别人来发言。

227
00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:23.060
And I mean, first of all, amazing, right?
我是说，首先，这太棒了，对吧？

228
00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:24.020
He's so sweet.
他真是太贴心了。

229
00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:24.380
Awesome.
太赞了。

230
00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:28.300
And so then Rainn said, I think Jenna should do it.
然后雷恩说，我觉得应该让珍娜去。

231
00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:33.260
And I feel like none of us really thought we were going to win because we'd won the year before.
我觉得我们当时都没觉得会赢，因为前一年我们刚拿过奖。

232
00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:34.720
And I said, oh, okay.
我说，哦，好吧。

233
00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:35.500
Yeah, sure.
行啊，没问题。

234
00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.100
I'll do it.
我来吧。

235
00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:36.980
And then we won.
然后我们真的赢了。

236
00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.340
And I had to give a speech at an award show.
我不得不去颁奖典礼上发表感言。

237
00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:41.560
And you did such a great job.
你当时表现得太棒了。

238
00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:44.120
You were so articulate and well-spoken.
你表达得非常清晰且得体。

239
00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:47.880
I was in awe because we didn't think we were going to win.
我当时惊呆了，因为我们根本没想过会赢。

240
00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.480
It was a total surprise.
完全是个惊喜。

241
00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:50.540
And then we won.
然后我们就赢了。

242
00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.180
And I'm like walking to the stage.
我当时正走上台。

243
00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:53.400
And I'm like, oh, my God.
我心想，天哪。

244
00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:56.380
Well, I know you guys are tired of me talking about being pregnant.
我知道你们听我谈论怀孕的事已经听腻了。

245
00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:58.040
But I was pregnant at that award show.
但我在那个颁奖典礼上时正怀着孕。

246
00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:02.860
And it's a very odd thing to be super huge and pregnant at an award show.
在颁奖典礼上挺着大肚子其实挺奇怪的。

247
00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:04.780
But you did such a great job.
但你当时表现得真的很棒。

248
00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:05.560
Thank you.
谢谢。

249
00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:11.500
I ended up kind of going down a rabbit hole of all the like cool things that happened for our show in 2008.
我最后深入挖掘了一下2008年我们剧组发生的那些酷事。

250
00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:12.780
It was a good year.
那真是美好的一年。

251
00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:13.860
It was a good year.
那一年过得不错。

252
00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:17.540
James Carey sent me the call sheet for this episode.
詹姆斯·凯里把这集的通告单发给了我。

253
00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:18.760
James-a-pedia.
“詹姆斯百科”。

254
00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:19.720
James-a-pedia.
“詹姆斯百科”。

255
00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:28.540
And on the call sheet, it said, there is a screening of Rainn Wilson's new movie, The Rocker, at Universal City Walk for the cast and crew.
通告单上写着，在环球城市大道有一场雷恩·威尔森新片《摇滚青春》的放映会，邀请全体演职人员参加。

256
00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:29.660
All are welcome.
欢迎所有人参加。

257
00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.860
So that was also happening.
所以当时还有这回事。

258
00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:33.940
That's a lot happening.
那发生的事情可真不少。

259
00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:34.720
All right.
好吧。

260
00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.200
Fast fact number three.
冷知识第三条。

261
00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:38.220
This episode is a baby shower.
这一集的主题是迎婴派对。

262
00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.780
So I'm going to tell you some stuff about baby showers.
所以我打算给你们讲讲关于迎婴派对的一些事。

263
00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:43.000
You did a deep dive on baby showers?
你对迎婴派对做了深入研究？

264
00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:43.400
I did.
没错。

265
00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:44.720
What is there to know?
那有什么好研究的？

266
00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:45.780
It's a baby coming.
不就是孩子要出生了嘛。

267
00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.080
Get some presents.
收点礼物。

268
00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.100
Get everyone ready.
让大家做好准备。

269
00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.400
What else is there to know?
还有什么好研究的？

270
00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:54.880
Well, baby showers are believed to date all the way back to the Egyptian and Greek civilizations.
嗯，据说迎婴派对的历史可以追溯到古埃及和古希腊文明时期。

271
00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:55.920
Whoa!
哇！

272
00:12:55.920 --> 00:13:02.000
But baby showers as we know them today began during the baby boom era of World War II.
但我们今天所熟知的迎婴派对，是始于二战后的婴儿潮时期。

273
00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:11.840
So traditionally, the baby shower was thrown by a close family member or a friend, and the mother-to-be opened gifts in a decorated chair.
按照传统，迎婴派对通常由亲近的家人或朋友举办，准妈妈会坐在装饰过的椅子上拆礼物。

274
00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.160
Well, Jan has a very decorated chair.
嗯，简确实有一把装饰得很华丽的椅子。

275
00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:15.180
I noticed.
我也注意到了。

276
00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:15.840
Yeah.
是啊。

277
00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.300
Thank you, party planning committee.
谢谢你，派对策划委员会。

278
00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:18.700
Thank you, Phyllis.
谢谢你，菲利斯。

279
00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:22.500
Well, I think Angela did it because Phyllis is making her do everything.
我觉得是安吉拉布置的，因为菲利斯什么活都丢给她干。

280
00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:23.980
So thank you, Angela.
所以谢谢你，安吉拉。

281
00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:24.860
Okay.
好吧。

282
00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:26.360
I don't know.
我不知道。

283
00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:27.420
Well, listen.
听着。

284
00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:31.340
Nowadays, we have all kinds of ways that we can celebrate a new baby.
如今，我们有各种各样的方式来庆祝新生命的到来。

285
00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:35.040
And here are some new updated baby showers.
这里有一些新式迎婴派对。

286
00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:36.840
A diaper shower.
尿布派对。

287
00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.920
That's where all you bring are diapers in different sizes.
就是大家只带各种尺寸的尿布来参加。

288
00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:46.460
It's like if you go to your baby shower, it's like you went to Costco and bought out all the diapers.
就像你去参加迎婴派对，结果像是去了好市多把所有的尿布都买光了一样。

289
00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.620
You just go home with every diaper because diapers are expensive.
你回家时会带上各种尿布，因为尿布很贵。

290
00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:50.920
What's the next one?
下一个是什么？

291
00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:52.420
Grandparents shower.
祖父母派对。

292
00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:53.180
Hmm?
嗯？

293
00:13:53.840 --> 00:14:01.480
This is a shower that you throw for the grandparents, and you give them stuff to keep at their house for when the baby comes over.
这是专门为祖父母举办的派对，送他们一些东西放在家里，好让孩子过去玩的时候用。

294
00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:03.300
Boo.
嘘。

295
00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:08.300
I love you, grandparents, but come on.
我爱你们，祖父母们，但别闹了。

296
00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:10.600
Grandparents, they love to go get that stuff.
祖父母们，他们很乐意去买那些东西。

297
00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:11.700
Yeah, I don't know.
是啊，我不知道。

298
00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.080
Here's another one.
还有这个。

299
00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:13.380
Okay.
好吧。

300
00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.320
I've heard of these.
我听说过这些。

301
00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:15.040
A sprinkle.
“小洒”派对。

302
00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:16.040
What?
什么？

303
00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:17.500
You don't have a baby shower.
你不能办产前派对。

304
00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:18.520
You have a sprinkle.
你得办“小洒”派对。

305
00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:19.640
It sounds like you're going pee.
听起来像你要去尿尿一样。

306
00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:20.440
It does.
确实是。

307
00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:31.400
This is a shower that you throw for your second or third or fourth babies to collect maybe some of the things if you are having a baby of a different gender.
这是为你第二个、第三个或第四个孩子举办的派对，如果你怀的是不同性别的孩子，可以借此收集一些必需品。

308
00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:32.240
Right, right.
对，对。

309
00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:33.780
Or if you need to refresh.
或者如果你需要更新一下装备。

310
00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:34.440
Oh, my God.
天哪。

311
00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:35.340
I just got it.
我刚明白过来了。

312
00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.280
A shower and a sprinkle.
产前派对（Shower）和“小洒”派对（Sprinkle）。

313
00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:37.740
Yeah.
是啊。

314
00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:38.900
It's not a full shower.
这不是正式的产前派对。

315
00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:40.140
It's just a sprinkle.
只是个“小洒”派对。

316
00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:42.460
Every time you say it, I just think of tinkling.
你每次说这个词，我就想到嘘嘘。

317
00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:43.580
I do, too.
我也是。

318
00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:44.780
All right.
好吧。

319
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.680
The final one is a sip and see.
最后一个是“品酒看娃”派对。

320
00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.420
Does this involve wine?
这包含喝酒吗？

321
00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:50.520
It does.
包含的。

322
00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:55.060
It is a celebration planned by the new parents after the baby has arrived.
这是新晋父母在宝宝出生后策划的庆祝活动。

323
00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.660
Oh, you sip and you get to see the baby.
哦，就是一边喝着酒，一边看宝宝。

324
00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:58.100
Yes.
没错。

325
00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:03.400
So I have to say what we are going to see in this episode is technically a sip and see.
所以我得说，我们这集要看的内容严格来说就是一场“品酒看娃”派对。

326
00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:04.360
You know what?
你知道吗？

327
00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:06.980
I have been to a sip and see, but I didn't even know it.
我参加过“品酒看娃”派对，但我当时甚至都不知道。

328
00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.040
I love the name sip and see.
我喜欢“品酒看娃”这个名字。

329
00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:09.880
Sip and see.
品酒看娃。

330
00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.960
Can I have a sip and see for my new puppy?
我可以为我的新小狗办一场“品酒看娃”派对吗？

331
00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:15.400
Can I do that?
我可以这样做吗？

332
00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:16.020
Yes.
可以。

333
00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:16.900
Okay, good.
好的，太好了。

334
00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:18.860
That's all I got, Ange.
我就这些了，安吉。

335
00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:19.800
Anything you want to add?
你有什么要补充的吗？

336
00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:21.200
Do you have a Kinsey tidbit today?
你今天有什么关于金西的小花絮吗？

337
00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:22.960
Well, here's a little Kinsey tidbit.
嗯，这里有个关于金西的小花絮。

338
00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:28.080
One of the things Erin said, which we have talked about before, is how long these scripts came in.
艾琳说过的一件事，我们之前也讨论过，就是这些剧本写出来时有多长。

339
00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:35.380
You know, they were pretty big episodes and then we would have to just chisel away and there was so much that didn't make it to the screen.
你知道，这些剧集篇幅很长，然后我们不得不删减，有很多内容都没能出现在屏幕上。

340
00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:39.460
For example, this episode came in at 49 pages, right?
比如，这一集剧本有49页，对吧？

341
00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:40.380
Wait, what?
等等，什么？

342
00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:43.860
The script for this was 49 pages?
这一集的剧本有49页？

343
00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:45.700
Yeah, 49 pages.
是的，49页。

344
00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:47.620
That's craziness.
太疯狂了。

345
00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:52.240
And you know how we've talked about how they would sort of rebuild the episodes in editing?
你知道我们讨论过他们如何在剪辑中重构剧集吗？

346
00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:55.580
Well, Erin had this quote that I absolutely loved.
艾琳有句名言，我特别喜欢。

347
00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:59.780
He said that Greg liked to rebuild the ship at sea.
他说格雷格喜欢在海上重修这艘船。

348
00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:00.800
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

349
00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:02.160
Isn't that such a great phrase?
这句话是不是很棒？

350
00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:03.080
I love that.
我太喜欢了。

351
00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:03.900
I just love that.
我真的太喜欢那个了。

352
00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:07.120
Yeah, they would get in the editor's room, man, and they would just carve it up.
是啊，他们会进剪辑室，伙计，然后大刀阔斧地剪辑。

353
00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:12.840
And I told him, I said, it's always interesting for me now that we have all these scripts, thank you, James,
我告诉他，我说，现在我们有了这么多剧本，谢谢你，詹姆斯，这对我来说总是很有趣，

354
00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:17.440
to see what makes it on the screen and what doesn't and how they move everything around.
看看什么能出现在屏幕上，什么不能，以及他们是如何调整一切的。

355
00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:21.200
And I'm always so happy with the final product, you know?
而且我对最终成品总是非常满意，你知道吗？

356
00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:23.080
But it's a cool thing to see.
但这确实是一件很酷的事情。

357
00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:27.060
But I thought that Greg likes to rebuild the ship at sea was like a great phrase.
但我认为格雷格说的“喜欢在海上重建船只”是一个很棒的短语。

358
00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.380
Well, I think those were really good fast facts.
嗯，我觉得那些速览事实真的很棒。

359
00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:31.440
And we've got some more Erin tidbits.
我们还有一些关于艾琳的趣闻。

360
00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.360
We should take a break and get into this episode.
我们该休息一下，进入这一集了。

361
00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:34.280
I like it.
我喜欢。

362
00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:43.890
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
请注意，所有WDNC的新老成员。

363
00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:47.730
I'm Melanie Sanders, and this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯，这是“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

364
00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:51.990
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们到了中年，意识到我们真的只是不再那么在乎了。

365
00:16:52.230 --> 00:17:00.070
Now we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling families, brain fog, and bat wings.
现在我们要互相帮助，去理解潮热、耳朵发痒、下巴长毛、琐碎的家庭、脑雾和蝴蝶袖。

366
00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:02.930
We are not alone, and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听到。

367
00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:04.850
So come join the WDNC.
所以快来加入WDNC吧。

368
00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:10.210
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get your podcaSt.
在任何你收听播客的地方，关注并收听梅兰妮·桑德斯的“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

369
00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:15.120
All right.
好的。

370
00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:16.140
We are back.
我们回来了。

371
00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:22.960
And you guys, at 12 seconds, everything you need to know about this episode is laid out by Jim.
伙计们，在12秒的时候，关于这一集你需要知道的一切都被吉姆列出来了。

372
00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:27.740
Jim has a dry erase board, and he's going to tell you everything you need to know about this episode.
吉姆有一个白板，他会告诉你关于这一集你需要知道的一切。

373
00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:29.520
Sam, can you play that clip?
萨姆，你能播放那个片段吗？

374
00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:37.500
Jan is about to have a baby with a sperm donor, and Michael is preparing for the birth of a watermelon with Dwight.
简即将通过精子捐赠生孩子，而迈克尔正准备和德怀特一起迎接一个西瓜的诞生。

375
00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:44.170
Now, this baby will be related to Michael through delusion.
现在，这个孩子将通过妄想与迈克尔产生联系。

376
00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:46.750
There you go.
就是这样。

377
00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:49.310
That pretty much sums it up.
这基本上总结了全部内容。

378
00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:50.330
That could have been the summary.
那本来可以作为总结的。

379
00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:51.110
I know, right?
我知道，对吧？

380
00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:53.850
When I saw that, I was like, well, that's everything you need to know.
当我看到那个时，我就想，好吧，这就是你需要知道的一切。

381
00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.810
Did you catch the Dwight?
你注意到德怀特了吗？

382
00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:56.270
I know.
我知道。

383
00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:59.550
I was about to say, and you got a real good Dwight in there.
我正要说，你那里模仿的德怀特真的很像。

384
00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:00.910
Well, it's true.
嗯，这是真的。

385
00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:02.370
Dwight is walking around.
德怀特走来走去。

386
00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:06.570
He's got a watermelon in his smock that he's wearing.
他穿着的罩衫里装着一个西瓜。

387
00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:07.090
Yeah.
是的。

388
00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:07.650
An apron?
围裙？

389
00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:10.510
They've fastened like a smock to hold the baby.
他们系了一个像罩衫一样的东西来固定那个“婴儿”。

390
00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:12.350
Yeah, the watermelon baby.
是的，西瓜宝宝。

391
00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:15.330
Do you have some Phil Shea trivia about this?
你有什么关于这个的菲尔·谢伊的冷知识吗？

392
00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:16.170
I do.
有的。

393
00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:16.750
Yay!
耶！

394
00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:19.250
I talked to Phil Shea for about an hour yesterday.
我昨天和菲尔·谢伊聊了大约一个小时。

395
00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:21.230
Prop master extraordinaire.
非凡的道具大师。

396
00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:21.810
I know.
我知道。

397
00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:27.830
And we are going to have him on for an extended interview because he has got just some great info and stories.
我们打算邀请他进行一次深度访谈，因为他有很多很棒的信息和故事。

398
00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:28.830
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

399
00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:30.490
We need to have Aaron Schur on, too.
我们也需要邀请亚伦·舒尔来。

400
00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:31.550
We really do.
确实需要。

401
00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:32.550
Let's load it up.
我们开始吧。

402
00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:33.070
All right.
好的。

403
00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:35.070
We had a fan question from Lisa W.
我们收到了一位粉丝Lisa W.的提问。

404
00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:40.450
How many watermelons were needed to do the practice birth scene with Michael and Dwight?
迈克尔和德怀特练习接生那场戏用了多少个西瓜？

405
00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:46.470
Phil said, in total, we used about 30 watermelons for this whole episode.
菲尔说，整集拍下来我们总共用了大约30个西瓜。

406
00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:49.510
Oh, because he straps it into the stroller later.
哦，因为他后来把西瓜绑在婴儿车里了。

407
00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:49.900
Yes.
没错。

408
00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:52.430
So for these scenes and for later.
所以是包括这些场景以及后面的戏份。

409
00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:58.770
And Phil said, you know, it's great living in Southern California because you can get watermelons all year.
菲尔还说，住在南加州真好，因为一年四季都能买到西瓜。

410
00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:00.370
So it wasn't a problem.
所以这不成问题。

411
00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:00.810
Okay.
好的。

412
00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:01.430
Yeah.
是啊。

413
00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:03.490
Fan catch from Evelyn V.
来自Evelyn V.的粉丝发现。

414
00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:12.150
said, at one minute, 41 seconds, I think I can see other stains from when the watermelon crashed into the ground on previous takes.
她说，在1分41秒处，我好像能看到之前拍摄时西瓜摔在地上留下的其他污渍。

415
00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:13.970
I looked at it.
我看了那个镜头。

416
00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:17.690
Evelyn, I think that's a stain from something else.
Evelyn，我觉得那应该是别的什么东西留下的污渍。

417
00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:19.270
I don't think it's a watermelon.
我不觉得那是西瓜留下的。

418
00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:25.590
I feel like, as Pam, I have walked up to the front of Michael's desk and I've looked down at my feet enough in scenes.
我觉得作为帕姆，我在戏里走到迈克尔办公桌前，低头看自己脚下的次数够多了。

419
00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:27.730
I recognize that stain.
我认得那个污渍。

420
00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.030
I don't know what that's from.
我不知道那是怎么弄的。

421
00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.990
I don't think it was watermelons.
我不觉得那是西瓜造成的。

422
00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:36.410
I don't know what to make of that other than maybe we should have splurged for new carpet.
除了觉得我们当时应该多花点钱换块新地毯之外，我也不知道该怎么解释。

423
00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.330
I think Michael needs new carpet.
我觉得迈克尔确实需要换块新地毯了。

424
00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:38.770
Yeah.
是啊。

425
00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:41.170
We had this letter from Ben M.
我们还收到了来自芝加哥的Ben M.的来信。

426
00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:42.030
in Chicago.
在芝加哥。

427
00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:50.510
I am an ER doctor and whenever I'm teaching medical students how to deliver a baby, I like to show them the cold open from this episode.
我是一名急诊科医生，每当我教医学生如何接生时，我都喜欢给他们看这一集的开场戏。

428
00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:51.350
Get out.
别逗了。

429
00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:51.970
Yes.
真的。

430
00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:57.070
This reinforces to them that newborns are very slippery.
这能让他们意识到新生儿非常滑。

431
00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:58.290
Oh, come on.
哦，得了吧。

432
00:19:58.350 --> 00:20:05.690
It helps teach them that you must always support the baby's head and neck and also hold an arm or a leg immediately after delivery.
这有助于教导他们，在接生后必须始终托住婴儿的头部和颈部，并立即抓住婴儿的手臂或腿。

433
00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:09.830
It is a very funny cold open, but also extremely accurate.
这不仅是一个非常有趣的开场，而且极其准确。

434
00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:10.850
Wow.
哇。

435
00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:11.650
Yeah.
是啊。

436
00:20:12.070 --> 00:20:15.430
Well, Aaron told me that this whole cold open was Greg's idea.
亚伦告诉我，整个开场戏都是格雷格的主意。

437
00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:17.410
The watermelon, the whole thing.
西瓜，整件事都是。

438
00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:17.710
Okay.
好吧。

439
00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:20.210
He had this whole idea and Aaron just ran with it.
他有了这个完整的构思，亚伦就照着去执行了。

440
00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:26.390
It's funny you say that because when I spoke with Phil, he said, I think Greg had an affinity for Gallagher.
你这么说很有趣，因为我和菲尔聊的时候，他说，我觉得格雷格对加拉格尔情有独钟。

441
00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:30.870
That's why you see so many watermelon gags on our show.
这就是为什么我们的节目里有那么多关于西瓜的梗。

442
00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:32.430
That is very funny.
那太搞笑了。

443
00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:32.850
Yeah.
是啊。

444
00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:35.630
The comedian Gallagher, he used to smash watermelons.
喜剧演员加拉格尔，他以前经常砸西瓜。

445
00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.910
And if you're on the front row, you just get splattered.
如果你坐在前排，就会被溅得满身都是。

446
00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:38.250
Yeah.
没错。

447
00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:39.870
I think that was it.
我想就是这样。

448
00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:45.450
Aaron told me, because after he spoke with you, he came to the DM.
亚伦告诉我的，因为他和你聊完之后，就给我发了私信。

449
00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:46.590
Oh, he found you.
哦，他找到你了。

450
00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:47.310
We DMed.
我们互发了私信。

451
00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:47.730
Oh, good.
哦，太好了。

452
00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:50.350
He said this cold open was the first thing they shot.
他说这段开场戏是他们拍摄的第一场戏。

453
00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:52.910
And it was his first time on set for The Office.
那也是他第一次来到《办公室》的片场。

454
00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:54.670
And he kept laughing out loud.
他当时一直忍不住大笑出声。

455
00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:58.990
And Greg had to say to him, Aaron, this is not Everybody Loves Raymond.
格雷格不得不对他说：亚伦，这不是《人人都爱雷蒙德》。

456
00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:00.010
It's not a live show.
这不是现场直播节目。

457
00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:01.230
You can't laugh out loud.
你不能大笑出声。

458
00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:02.710
And he was like, oh, no.
他当时反应是：哦，不。

459
00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:03.430
Yes.
没错。

460
00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:07.390
He told me that it became a thing he became very self-conscious about because he'd only
他告诉我，这让他变得非常不自在，因为他之前只

461
00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:10.990
ever worked in four camera where they encourage you to laugh and laugh and laugh.
在四机位拍摄的剧组工作过，那种环境鼓励你大笑特笑。

462
00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:14.390
And then he had to start suppressing the laugh and suppressing the laugh.
然后他不得不开始强忍笑意，一直忍着。

463
00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:19.830
And he said after a long day of work and suppressing the laugh, he would go home and just burp
他说在辛苦工作了一整天并强忍笑意后，他回家后就会

464
00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:20.630
constantly.
不停地打嗝。

465
00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:21.970
He told me that, too.
他也跟我说过这件事。

466
00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:26.430
He had given himself, like, some type of indigestion from holding in laughter all day.
他因为整天憋着笑，搞得自己好像得了某种消化不良一样。

467
00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:28.110
Oh.
噢。

468
00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:32.470
Well, you guys, this was very hard to watch without laughing for all of us.
好吧，伙计们，我们所有人看这段的时候都很难忍住不笑。

469
00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:38.230
And if you go to one minute, 11 seconds, Phyllis had to put her head down because she was laughing
如果你看到一分十一秒，菲利斯不得不低下头，因为她笑得

470
00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:38.850
so hard.
太厉害了。

471
00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:43.250
The shot of the bullpen reacting.
那个办公区反应的镜头。

472
00:21:43.630 --> 00:21:43.830
Yeah.
是啊。

473
00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:45.770
Was so funny to me.
我觉得太好笑了。

474
00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:48.930
Well, there is a lot in this episode that we could not get through.
好吧，这一集里有很多我们没法顺利拍完的戏份。

475
00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:50.050
Oh, man.
天哪。

476
00:21:50.310 --> 00:21:51.370
The conference room.
会议室那场。

477
00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:52.030
We'll get there.
我们待会儿会讲到。

478
00:21:53.110 --> 00:21:57.510
I think we should get to the party planning committee now because they have been very
我觉得我们现在应该聊聊派对策划委员会了，因为她们一直

479
00:21:57.510 --> 00:22:00.130
busy decorating the conference room for the shower.
忙着为迎婴派对装饰会议室。

480
00:22:00.490 --> 00:22:00.650
Yeah.
没错。

481
00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:02.430
They have two bowls of M&Ms.
她们准备了两碗M&M豆。

482
00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:07.970
So I talked to Erin about this and I said, who came up with Astrid and Chevy?
所以我跟艾琳聊过这个，我问他：阿斯特丽德和切维这两个名字是谁想出来的？

483
00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.270
And he said Astrid was definitely Greg.
他说阿斯特丽德肯定是格雷格的主意。

484
00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:12.950
He thought it'd be funny to see that name on an M&M.
他觉得在M&M豆上看到那个名字会很有趣。

485
00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:17.950
And then Chevy, he couldn't remember who came up with that.
至于切维，他不记得是谁想出来的了。

486
00:22:18.130 --> 00:22:20.190
He said he thinks the room kind of pitched names.
他说他觉得当时是编剧室里大家一起提议的。

487
00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:21.050
It's funny.
真有意思。

488
00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:25.130
When I saw the bowls of M&Ms with the names, that was like a really popular thing.
当我看到那些写着名字的M&M豆碗时，那在当时真的很流行。

489
00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:28.510
It might still be popular where you can get these personalized M&Ms.
可能现在依然流行，你可以定制这种M&M豆。

490
00:22:28.590 --> 00:22:29.610
Oh, I went to the website.
哦，我上过那个网站。

491
00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:30.770
It's still a whole thing.
这依然是个很火的东西。

492
00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:33.650
High school graduation, anniversaries.
高中毕业、周年纪念什么的。

493
00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:36.510
And I did this for my parents, my parents' anniversary.
我为我父母的结婚纪念日也做过这个。

494
00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:38.410
I got M&Ms with their names on it.
我定制了印有他们名字的M&M豆。

495
00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:46.490
Well, when we did the Jim and Pam wedding episode, Greg threw the cast a viewing party that
嗯，当我们拍吉姆和帕姆的婚礼那一集时，格雷格为剧组成员举办了一个观看派对，

496
00:22:46.490 --> 00:22:52.370
was kind of like a little mini reception and he had bowls of M&Ms that said Jim and Pam.
就像一个小型的招待会，他准备了印有吉姆和帕姆名字的M&M豆。

497
00:22:52.670 --> 00:22:54.350
He clearly was a big fan.
他显然是这个的忠实粉丝。

498
00:22:54.530 --> 00:22:56.670
He loved that you could personalize an M&M.
他很喜欢这种可以定制M&M豆的功能。

499
00:22:56.690 --> 00:22:57.050
I know.
我知道。

500
00:22:57.470 --> 00:22:59.670
Well, they've gotten the name wrong though.
不过，她们把名字弄错了。

501
00:22:59.890 --> 00:23:02.510
The party planning committee has Ass Turd.
派对策划委员会里有个叫“Ass Turd”的。

502
00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:04.810
Phyllis is like, that can't be right.
菲利斯觉得，这名字肯定不对。

503
00:23:05.450 --> 00:23:08.110
Angela's like, Michael wrote down Ass Turd.
安吉拉说，迈克尔写的就是“Ass Turd”。

504
00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:12.530
And Michael said, yeah, it's like the name of a Viking princess.
迈克尔说，没错，这就像是个维京公主的名字。

505
00:23:13.090 --> 00:23:17.530
So, of course, I had to research Ass Turd.
所以，我当然得去研究一下“Ass Turd”。

506
00:23:17.670 --> 00:23:19.450
I didn't research Ass Turd.
我其实没去研究“Ass Turd”。

507
00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:21.430
And he is right.
而且他是对的。

508
00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:22.750
Michael is right.
迈克尔是对的。

509
00:23:23.030 --> 00:23:28.210
According to the internet, Ass Turd has Norse, Danish, and Swedish roots.
根据互联网的说法，“Ass Turd”有挪威、丹麦和瑞典语源。

510
00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:31.930
It can mean godly strength or divine beauty.
它可以意为神圣的力量或绝世的美貌。

511
00:23:32.150 --> 00:23:37.450
And the name Ass Turd has been used by Norway's royal family for hundreds of years.
而且“Ass Turd”这个名字已经被挪威王室沿用了几百年。

512
00:23:38.110 --> 00:23:40.190
You know, Michael is annoyed by their effort.
你知道，迈克尔对她们的努力感到很恼火。

513
00:23:41.070 --> 00:23:45.530
He says, Phyllis, we gave you a whole golden shower.
他说，菲利斯，我们给了你一场盛大的“黄金雨”。

514
00:23:45.670 --> 00:23:47.070
I want my golden shower.
我想要我的“黄金雨”。

515
00:23:47.270 --> 00:23:47.870
He does.
他确实这么说了。

516
00:23:48.250 --> 00:23:52.150
And then he has this talking head where he says he's going to love this baby,
然后他有个单人采访，说他会爱这个孩子，

517
00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:56.410
even if it isn't his, like that dog that nursed the tiger cub.
即使不是他亲生的，就像那只喂养虎崽的狗一样。

518
00:23:56.710 --> 00:23:57.230
Right?
对吧？

519
00:23:57.650 --> 00:23:59.350
Bizarre, but also beautiful.
离奇，但也挺美好的。

520
00:23:59.550 --> 00:24:00.050
It happens.
这种事确实会发生。

521
00:24:00.690 --> 00:24:01.950
Jenna, I looked it up.
珍娜，我查过了。

522
00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:05.950
And there are so many stories of dogs nursing tigers.
确实有很多关于狗喂养老虎的故事。

523
00:24:05.950 --> 00:24:11.170
But the one that caught my eye was on the Today Show in August of 2008.
但最吸引我的是2008年8月《今日秀》里的那个。

524
00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:13.170
That's when we shot this episode.
那正是我们拍摄这一集的时候。

525
00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:13.770
I know.
我知道。

526
00:24:13.770 --> 00:24:18.830
And there was a safari park in Kansas with a white tiger named Sassy.
当时堪萨斯州有个野生动物园，里面有只叫“Sassy”的白虎。

527
00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:19.590
Oh.
噢。

528
00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:23.330
Who had cubs, but she was too sassy to nurse them.
它生了幼崽，但它太“Sassy”（傲慢）了，不肯喂奶。

529
00:24:23.610 --> 00:24:23.950
Okay.
好吧。

530
00:24:24.290 --> 00:24:26.770
So a golden retriever stepped in, Isabella.
于是，一只金毛寻回犬挺身而出，它叫伊莎贝拉。

531
00:24:27.130 --> 00:24:29.310
Well, I would expect that from a golden retriever.
嗯，我倒觉得金毛干出这种事很正常。

532
00:24:29.390 --> 00:24:29.970
I really would.
真的。

533
00:24:30.130 --> 00:24:31.050
What a good dog.
真是只好狗。

534
00:24:31.050 --> 00:24:35.250
Anyway, it just cracked me up that on the Today Show, there was a whole thing about
总之，让我觉得好笑的是，《今日秀》专门做了一期关于

535
00:24:35.250 --> 00:24:36.930
Sassy and Isabella.
Sassy和伊莎贝拉的节目。

536
00:24:37.070 --> 00:24:39.070
And I think it ended up in our episode.
我觉得这事儿最后被写进了我们的剧集里。

537
00:24:39.310 --> 00:24:40.130
Clearly it did.
显然是这样。

538
00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:42.630
Michael is going to bark orders at Phyllis.
迈克尔要对菲利斯发号施令了。

539
00:24:43.090 --> 00:24:44.390
She's doing a talking head.
她正在做单人采访。

540
00:24:44.630 --> 00:24:46.990
I was supposed to be glaring at her in the background.
我本该在背景里怒视她的。

541
00:24:47.270 --> 00:24:51.370
And if you go to four minutes, 11 seconds, you can see me talking to Andy.
如果你看到4分11秒，能看到我在和安迪说话。

542
00:24:51.570 --> 00:24:54.310
And I'm so delighted that Phyllis is messing up.
我当时特别高兴看到菲利斯搞砸了。

543
00:24:54.490 --> 00:24:58.190
And then Michael walks in and kind of yells at her and says, make the party, make the party.
然后迈克尔走进来，冲她吼道，去办派对，去办派对。

544
00:24:58.190 --> 00:25:01.110
And then he leaves and Phyllis starts pumping the balloon.
他离开后，菲利斯开始给气球充气。

545
00:25:01.490 --> 00:25:05.830
Well, Steve improvised, walking back in and saying, pump it, pump it.
其实，史蒂夫即兴发挥，走回来喊道：充气，充气。

546
00:25:05.930 --> 00:25:06.390
He did?
真的吗？

547
00:25:06.670 --> 00:25:06.950
He did.
真的。

548
00:25:07.090 --> 00:25:07.910
That was all improv.
那全是即兴表演。

549
00:25:08.270 --> 00:25:09.650
We just started cracking up.
我们当时都笑喷了。

550
00:25:09.730 --> 00:25:12.490
I thought I could see you starting to break in the background of that.
我当时就觉得在背景里看到你快要憋不住笑了。

551
00:25:12.490 --> 00:25:12.690
Yeah.
是啊。

552
00:25:12.810 --> 00:25:14.290
And Phyllis is starting to break too.
菲利斯也快要破功了。

553
00:25:14.810 --> 00:25:21.470
So now Jim is at his desk and Pam is trying to tell him this story.
现在吉姆坐在办公桌前，帕姆正试着跟他讲这个故事。

554
00:25:21.770 --> 00:25:22.790
I loved this.
我超喜欢这段。

555
00:25:22.930 --> 00:25:23.870
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

556
00:25:24.050 --> 00:25:27.810
When she's like, Sarah Kaya comes in and he goes, oh, wait, Sarah Kaya comes in.
当她说“莎拉·卡亚进来了”，然后他说“哦，等等，莎拉·卡亚进来了”。

557
00:25:27.810 --> 00:25:31.590
And she's like, no, Sarah Kaya comes in.
她说“不，是莎拉·卡亚进来了”。

558
00:25:32.350 --> 00:25:37.510
And then at the very end of the scene, when Dwight's like, who's Sarah Kaya comes in?
最后在场景结尾，德怀特问“谁是莎拉·卡亚进来了？”的时候。

559
00:25:37.770 --> 00:25:38.970
That was improvised.
那是即兴发挥的。

560
00:25:39.250 --> 00:25:39.870
It was?
真的吗？

561
00:25:40.090 --> 00:25:40.850
Rain improvised that.
那是雷恩即兴加的。

562
00:25:40.970 --> 00:25:41.790
That's not in the script.
剧本里没有那句。

563
00:25:42.150 --> 00:25:43.250
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

564
00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:48.030
I watched this and I feel like I have had these conversations.
我看了这段，感觉自己也经历过这种对话。

565
00:25:48.250 --> 00:25:48.570
Yes.
没错。

566
00:25:48.730 --> 00:25:49.530
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

567
00:25:49.790 --> 00:25:53.290
And I love the line when she's like, why can't you just be in art school with me?
我特别喜欢她说“你为什么就不能跟我一起去上艺术学校呢？”那句台词。

568
00:25:54.430 --> 00:25:56.590
Because she's trying so hard to tell him the story.
因为她正努力地想把故事讲给他听。

569
00:25:56.950 --> 00:26:01.430
And, you know, this is the beginning of this storyline with Jim and Pam, where we're going
你知道，这是吉姆和帕姆这条故事线的开端，我们要展现的是

570
00:26:01.430 --> 00:26:06.830
to show that this distance has gone on for a while and maybe they're not connecting as
这种距离感已经持续了一段时间，也许他们不像过去那样

571
00:26:06.830 --> 00:26:08.390
easily as they used to.
能轻松地产生共鸣了。

572
00:26:08.550 --> 00:26:10.570
You know, long distance relationships are hard.
你知道，异地恋是很艰难的。

573
00:26:10.710 --> 00:26:15.650
And particularly when the people involved in your new life, the other person doesn't know.
尤其是当你新生活里的人，对方完全不认识的时候。

574
00:26:15.930 --> 00:26:17.250
And it's kind of hard to keep track.
而且很难跟上对方的节奏。

575
00:26:17.250 --> 00:26:18.410
Oh, yes.
哦，确实。

576
00:26:18.590 --> 00:26:21.290
I mean, we experience this all the time when we go on locations.
我是说，我们去外地拍摄时经常遇到这种情况。

577
00:26:21.870 --> 00:26:25.810
Or I remember Lee went on location to shoot a movie and he was directing a film.
我记得李去外地拍电影，他在执导那部片子。

578
00:26:26.110 --> 00:26:31.410
And he's trying to tell me this hilarious story about some prop mishap that happened.
他想跟我讲一个关于道具事故的爆笑故事。

579
00:26:31.570 --> 00:26:33.890
And everyone was laughing about these prop glasses.
当时大家都在笑那些道具眼镜的事。

580
00:26:34.270 --> 00:26:36.850
And I'm just like, I don't know who any of these people are.
而我却一脸茫然，因为我根本不知道那些人是谁。

581
00:26:36.990 --> 00:26:42.510
And what's really hard about it is that I like to be able to imagine the people or where
最难受的是，我喜欢在脑海里想象那些人或者他们所在的

582
00:26:42.510 --> 00:26:43.110
they are.
地方。

583
00:26:43.810 --> 00:26:46.510
And we've talked about this when we get to a new place.
我们聊过这个，每当我们去到一个新地方。

584
00:26:46.510 --> 00:26:50.470
Send me a video of where you are so that when I'm talking to you, I know what your little
给我发个视频看看你在哪，这样当你跟我说话时，我就知道你的小

585
00:26:50.470 --> 00:26:53.090
apartment looks like or I know what your room looks like.
公寓长什么样，或者知道你的房间是什么样。

586
00:26:53.170 --> 00:26:54.410
Yeah, I have to have that.
没错，我必须得看到。

587
00:26:54.610 --> 00:26:57.370
Otherwise, I'm a little unsettled because I can't picture where you are.
否则我会有点不安，因为我无法想象你身处何处。

588
00:26:57.670 --> 00:26:57.990
Yes.
是的。

589
00:26:58.170 --> 00:27:02.290
So I feel like that's what Pam and Jim are up against right now.
所以我感觉这就是帕姆和吉姆现在所面临的问题。

590
00:27:02.570 --> 00:27:04.250
Yeah, he doesn't know her world.
是啊，他不了解她的世界。

591
00:27:04.250 --> 00:27:07.290
And it's some of that location situation kind of stuff.
这有点像那种异地拍摄的情况。

592
00:27:07.750 --> 00:27:09.070
I love the next scene.
我喜欢接下来的那个场景。

593
00:27:10.750 --> 00:27:12.010
I love it so much.
我太喜欢了。

594
00:27:12.010 --> 00:27:18.630
Angela is preparing this poster board full of baby photos because they're going to play
安吉拉正在准备一块贴满婴儿照片的展板，因为他们要玩

595
00:27:18.630 --> 00:27:23.130
a game where you have to guess which baby photo belongs to which employee.
一个游戏，猜哪张婴儿照片属于哪位员工。

596
00:27:23.570 --> 00:27:28.270
And Andy comes in and he mistakes Phyllis's baby photo for Angela.
安迪走进来，把菲利斯的婴儿照片错认成了安吉拉的。

597
00:27:28.650 --> 00:27:29.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

598
00:27:29.390 --> 00:27:31.690
Will you please tell me about shooting this scene, Angela?
安吉拉，你能跟我讲讲拍这场戏的情况吗？

599
00:27:32.250 --> 00:27:35.330
Well, one of the reasons I storm off is because I started to laugh.
嗯，我之所以气冲冲地走开，是因为我当时快笑场了。

600
00:27:35.550 --> 00:27:36.130
I could tell.
我看得出来。

601
00:27:36.130 --> 00:27:40.310
That was me trying to get out of there before you saw me laughing on camera.
那是我在镜头前笑出声被你发现之前，试图溜走的样子。

602
00:27:40.490 --> 00:27:41.550
So here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

603
00:27:41.770 --> 00:27:43.290
Greg directed this episode, right?
这一集是格雷格导演的，对吧？

604
00:27:43.450 --> 00:27:47.290
And he said, you guys, can you bring in your actual baby photos?
他说，伙计们，你们能带上自己小时候的照片吗？

605
00:27:47.610 --> 00:27:50.470
And he said, if you don't have a baby photo, it could be like when you're a toddler.
他说，如果没有婴儿时期的照片，幼儿时期的也行。

606
00:27:50.790 --> 00:27:52.950
Just can I get photos of you guys when you were little?
就是能不能给我一些你们小时候的照片？

607
00:27:53.150 --> 00:27:54.450
And we did, right?
我们就照做了，对吧？

608
00:27:54.450 --> 00:27:56.410
Yes, we got a lot of fan mail about that.
没错，我们收到了很多关于那件事的粉丝来信。

609
00:27:56.410 --> 00:27:59.130
Were these actual photos of the cast?
那些真的是演员们本人的照片吗？

610
00:27:59.550 --> 00:28:00.170
They were.
是的。

611
00:28:00.390 --> 00:28:00.590
Yeah.
没错。

612
00:28:06.270 --> 00:28:10.050
Everyone else is an actual baby photo from their childhood.
其他人的照片都是他们童年时期的真实照片。

613
00:28:10.310 --> 00:28:11.290
Including Amy Ryan.
包括艾米·莱恩的。

614
00:28:11.470 --> 00:28:11.990
She's up there.
她也在上面。

615
00:28:12.190 --> 00:28:12.550
Yes.
是的。

616
00:28:13.190 --> 00:28:14.430
And so is Mindy.
敏迪的也在。

617
00:28:14.550 --> 00:28:15.830
I mean, we're all on the board.
我是说，我们都在那块板子上。

618
00:28:15.930 --> 00:28:16.070
Yeah.
是的。

619
00:28:16.290 --> 00:28:16.710
We're all on the board.
我们都在那块板子上。

620
00:28:17.090 --> 00:28:18.230
Jenna, what did I bring in today?
珍娜，我今天带了什么来？

621
00:28:18.310 --> 00:28:19.090
Do you want to share with them?
你想和大家分享一下吗？

622
00:28:19.270 --> 00:28:21.710
You brought in your baby photo.
你带了你的婴儿照。

623
00:28:21.910 --> 00:28:26.730
The one that was on the board with your little hand up on your little chubby cheek.
就是板子上那张，你的一只小手托着胖乎乎的小脸蛋的那张。

624
00:28:26.910 --> 00:28:27.450
I know.
我知道。

625
00:28:27.830 --> 00:28:28.550
I know.
我知道。

626
00:28:28.750 --> 00:28:30.350
You guys, it's really me.
伙计们，那真的是我。

627
00:28:30.490 --> 00:28:31.790
I get asked this all the time.
我经常被问到这个问题。

628
00:28:31.930 --> 00:28:35.310
And my mom, I called my mom and I said, mom, we're doing the baby shower episode.
我当时给我妈打电话说，妈，我们要拍“迎婴派对”那一集了。

629
00:28:35.310 --> 00:28:36.710
And it's my baby photo.
那张是我的婴儿照。

630
00:28:36.870 --> 00:28:38.490
And I want to know everything about it.
我想了解关于它的一切。

631
00:28:38.570 --> 00:28:42.070
She said, oh, I have several more of that same day where we put you in different poses.
她说，哦，那天拍的照片还有好几张，我们当时给你摆了不同的姿势。

632
00:28:43.350 --> 00:28:45.030
Oh, so there's more.
哦，所以还有更多照片。

633
00:28:45.250 --> 00:28:47.030
But here's what my mom said.
但我妈是这么说的。

634
00:28:47.090 --> 00:28:52.150
She took me to JCPenney's at the Acadiana Shopping Mall in Lafayette, Louisiana.
她带我去了路易斯安那州拉斐特市阿卡迪亚纳购物中心的杰西潘尼百货。

635
00:28:52.570 --> 00:28:54.410
I was around six months old.
我当时大概六个月大。

636
00:28:54.650 --> 00:28:57.670
And apparently, I was born with just a ton of hair.
显然，我一出生就头发浓密。

637
00:28:57.830 --> 00:28:59.350
And it was sort of an auburn brown.
颜色是那种红棕色。

638
00:28:59.630 --> 00:29:01.830
She said I had so much hair.
她说我的头发特别多。

639
00:29:02.130 --> 00:29:04.830
Just right out of the gate, I had tons of hair.
刚出生时就有一头浓密的头发。

640
00:29:05.430 --> 00:29:08.150
And so she tried to style it for the photo.
所以她试着为拍照做个造型。

641
00:29:08.370 --> 00:29:11.650
I was like, mom, you gave me like a mohawk with bangs.
我说，妈，你给我弄了个带刘海的莫霍克发型。

642
00:29:12.290 --> 00:29:15.730
So yeah, she said she had tried to put a little ribbon at the top.
所以她说她本来试着在头顶扎个小丝带。

643
00:29:15.930 --> 00:29:17.050
That would have made more sense.
那样看起来会更合理些。

644
00:29:17.270 --> 00:29:17.490
Right.
没错。

645
00:29:17.650 --> 00:29:19.810
But I don't know, it fell out or something.
但我不知道，可能是掉了还是怎么的。

646
00:29:20.010 --> 00:29:23.270
And then they propped me up on my hand like that.
然后他们就把我像那样撑在手上。

647
00:29:24.350 --> 00:29:28.570
It's so funny because I remember those photo studio photo shoots.
真有意思，因为我也记得那些照相馆的拍摄经历。

648
00:29:28.770 --> 00:29:30.630
That was a thing of my childhood as well.
那也是我童年的一部分。

649
00:29:30.630 --> 00:29:33.390
And they would have these carpeted blocks.
他们会有那种铺着地毯的方块道具。

650
00:29:33.630 --> 00:29:33.910
Yes.
是的。

651
00:29:34.130 --> 00:29:37.070
And you would like be propped up on a little carpeted block.
你还得被垫在一个铺着地毯的小方块上。

652
00:29:37.310 --> 00:29:39.870
I'm propped up because I can't sit yet, really.
我被垫着是因为我其实还坐不稳。

653
00:29:40.890 --> 00:29:42.370
Anyway, there you go.
总之，就是这样。

654
00:29:42.510 --> 00:29:44.410
That's my actual baby photo, you guys.
伙计们，那真的是我小时候的照片。

655
00:29:44.670 --> 00:29:49.970
Well, since mine wasn't on the board, I tell you what, I'll post mine on the Office Ladies pod.
好吧，既然我的照片没在板子上，我告诉你们，我会把我的照片发到《办公室女士》的播客上。

656
00:29:49.970 --> 00:29:51.670
So you can see me as a baby too.
这样你们也能看到我小时候的样子了。

657
00:29:51.810 --> 00:29:52.110
Yes.
没错。

658
00:29:52.210 --> 00:29:55.790
And I'll ask my mom if she can find any other photos from that particular photo shoot.
我还会问问我妈，看她能不能找到那次拍摄的其他照片。

659
00:29:56.910 --> 00:30:10.270
As Michael is preparing for Jan's arrival, he needs to tell Holly that he's going to be kind of cold to her today because he needs to protect Jan's feelings.
迈克尔在为简的到来做准备时，他需要告诉霍莉，他今天得对她冷淡一点，因为他需要顾及简的感受。

660
00:30:10.470 --> 00:30:11.970
Jan's bloated feelings.
简那浮肿的感受。

661
00:30:12.210 --> 00:30:12.390
Yeah.
是啊。

662
00:30:12.550 --> 00:30:14.090
Because Jan is going to come in.
因为简马上就要来了。

663
00:30:14.170 --> 00:30:16.650
She's going to be so unattractive.
她看起来会非常没有吸引力。

664
00:30:16.850 --> 00:30:18.490
And Holly is very attractive.
而霍莉非常有吸引力。

665
00:30:18.710 --> 00:30:20.710
And yeah, he just wants to be sensitive.
所以，他只是想表现得体贴一点。

666
00:30:20.710 --> 00:30:22.670
So he warns her.
于是他提前警告了她。

667
00:30:23.010 --> 00:30:25.510
But then Jan arrives.
但随后简到了。

668
00:30:25.970 --> 00:30:27.350
She's not pregnant.
她并没有怀孕。

669
00:30:27.650 --> 00:30:29.090
She has a baby.
她已经生了孩子。

670
00:30:29.410 --> 00:30:30.730
And she looks amazing.
而且她看起来棒极了。

671
00:30:31.050 --> 00:30:31.530
Yeah.
是啊。

672
00:30:31.850 --> 00:30:33.110
But she's had the baby.
但她已经把孩子生下来了。

673
00:30:33.470 --> 00:30:37.890
We had a fan question from Brittany Y., Sarah M., and many more.
我们收到了布列塔尼·Y、莎拉·M以及许多其他人的粉丝提问。

674
00:30:38.070 --> 00:30:40.690
Who is the baby that played Astrid?
饰演阿斯特丽德的那个婴儿是谁？

675
00:30:40.930 --> 00:30:43.610
I will tell you, thanks to Jamesopedia.
多亏了《詹姆斯百科》，我来告诉你们。

676
00:30:44.130 --> 00:30:48.290
First of all, you know, babies are played by many babies.
首先，你们知道，婴儿角色通常由好几个婴儿轮流扮演。

677
00:30:48.290 --> 00:30:48.870
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

678
00:30:49.530 --> 00:30:50.950
Sometimes they're a set of twins.
有时是一对双胞胎。

679
00:30:51.130 --> 00:30:58.030
Like in the case of Cece, Cece was this set of twins, and it was the same twin girls all through the show.
就像西西的情况，西西是由一对双胞胎扮演的，而且整个剧集里都是那对双胞胎女孩。

680
00:30:58.310 --> 00:31:00.750
They were absolute sweethearts, and I loved them.
她们绝对是小甜心，我非常喜欢她们。

681
00:31:01.150 --> 00:31:07.630
But sometimes, especially with a baby this little, it's like three babies, five babies, lots of babies.
但有时，特别是对于这么小的婴儿，可能需要三个、五个，甚至更多的婴儿来轮换。

682
00:31:07.770 --> 00:31:11.190
Oh, Philip was several different babies and then a different toddler.
哦，菲利普就是由好几个不同的婴儿，后来又换成了一个不同的幼儿扮演的。

683
00:31:11.730 --> 00:31:12.150
Yes.
没错。

684
00:31:12.390 --> 00:31:16.390
So this is because there are rules about babies working on a set.
这是因为片场对婴儿工作有严格的规定。

685
00:31:16.390 --> 00:31:18.630
They can only work for like 20 minutes.
他们每次只能工作大约20分钟。

686
00:31:18.990 --> 00:31:20.330
And I think that's a good thing.
我觉得这挺好的。

687
00:31:20.510 --> 00:31:20.930
Yes.
是的。

688
00:31:21.910 --> 00:31:26.910
Also, if you have a baby and one of them's fussy, you can swap them out for a different baby.
而且，如果你有几个婴儿，其中一个闹脾气了，你就可以换另一个上场。

689
00:31:27.110 --> 00:31:28.110
They're all dressed the same.
他们都穿着一样的衣服。

690
00:31:28.230 --> 00:31:30.790
You go backstage and there's like six babies in the same outfit.
你走到后台，会看到大概六个穿着同样衣服的婴儿。

691
00:31:31.290 --> 00:31:36.710
So Astrid was played first by a set of twins and another baby.
所以，阿斯特丽德最初是由一对双胞胎和另一个婴儿共同扮演的。

692
00:31:36.950 --> 00:31:38.270
Here's the crazy thing.
最疯狂的事情来了。

693
00:31:38.450 --> 00:31:41.770
The twins' names were Matthew and Joey Levinson.
那对双胞胎的名字叫马修·莱文森和乔伊·莱文森。

694
00:31:42.450 --> 00:31:42.970
Crazy.
太疯狂了。

695
00:31:43.270 --> 00:31:43.550
Right?
对吧？

696
00:31:43.550 --> 00:31:45.890
And they were playing Jan Levinson's baby.
他们竟然在扮演简·莱文森的孩子。

697
00:31:46.110 --> 00:31:46.450
Yes.
没错。

698
00:31:46.750 --> 00:31:49.010
The other baby was Harvey Green.
另一个婴儿叫哈维·格林。

699
00:31:49.210 --> 00:31:52.430
So her babies were the Levinson Green babies.
所以她的孩子就是“莱文森-格林”宝宝。

700
00:31:52.750 --> 00:31:52.930
Okay.
好吧。

701
00:31:53.870 --> 00:31:54.590
All right.
好的。

702
00:31:54.730 --> 00:31:56.090
And then that was on one day.
那是其中一天的事。

703
00:31:56.370 --> 00:32:00.410
The other day, we had a set of triplets playing Astrid.
另一天，我们找了一组三胞胎来扮演阿斯特丽德。

704
00:32:00.770 --> 00:32:03.670
They were Chase, Chloe, and Juliet Purcell.
她们是蔡斯、克洛伊和朱丽叶·珀塞尔。

705
00:32:04.190 --> 00:32:05.890
So those are all the babies.
所以这些就是所有的宝宝了。

706
00:32:05.990 --> 00:32:07.170
We also had a fake baby.
我们还有一个假宝宝。

707
00:32:07.390 --> 00:32:08.830
We did have a fake baby.
我们确实有个假宝宝。

708
00:32:08.930 --> 00:32:09.070
Yeah.
没错。

709
00:32:09.070 --> 00:32:14.410
And it's really funny because if you look at the call sheet, scene by scene, it'll say
这真的很有趣，因为如果你看通告单，每一场戏都会写着

710
00:32:14.830 --> 00:32:16.450
real baby or fake baby.
真宝宝还是假宝宝。

711
00:32:16.870 --> 00:32:18.430
Like what we're using in the scene.
就是我们在那场戏里用的道具。

712
00:32:18.570 --> 00:32:19.850
And they would stagger them, right?
他们会错开使用，对吧？

713
00:32:19.950 --> 00:32:21.770
Because the babies could only work for 20 minutes.
因为宝宝们每次只能工作20分钟。

714
00:32:22.170 --> 00:32:25.690
So you'd have a scene with a real baby and then a scene with a fake baby.
所以你会看到一场戏用真宝宝，下一场戏就用假宝宝。

715
00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:30.530
Well, Michael walks out of the kitchen and he sees Jan with the baby.
迈克尔从厨房走出来，看到简抱着宝宝。

716
00:32:31.090 --> 00:32:32.430
I can't imagine how he felt.
我无法想象他当时是什么感觉。

717
00:32:32.650 --> 00:32:35.010
He'd been to all of his birthing classes with her.
他明明和她一起上了所有的产前辅导课。

718
00:32:35.510 --> 00:32:38.230
And then he was sort of left out of this big moment.
结果他却被排除在这个重要时刻之外。

719
00:32:38.870 --> 00:32:40.810
And he confronts Jan about it.
于是他为此质问了简。

720
00:32:41.030 --> 00:32:43.830
This is one of my favorite couplets of dialogue from the whole episode.
这是整集中我最喜欢的对白之一。

721
00:32:44.330 --> 00:32:44.770
Okay.
好的。

722
00:32:45.010 --> 00:32:46.090
It's so rich.
内容太丰富了。

723
00:32:46.290 --> 00:32:48.230
Michael says, why didn't you call me?
迈克尔问，你为什么不叫我？

724
00:32:48.350 --> 00:32:49.230
I could have helped.
我本可以帮忙的。

725
00:32:49.510 --> 00:32:53.390
Jan said, well, the birth instructor thought it wasn't a good idea for you to be there.
简说，产前辅导老师觉得你在场不太好。

726
00:32:53.390 --> 00:33:00.850
So Michael says, oh man, him, that guy, he had no sense of humor and I proved him wrong
迈克尔就说，天哪，那家伙，他一点幽默感都没有，我用各种方式

727
00:33:00.850 --> 00:33:02.230
in so many ways.
证明了他错了。

728
00:33:02.630 --> 00:33:05.270
And it just made me think about these classes.
这让我不禁想到了这些课程。

729
00:33:05.510 --> 00:33:11.230
I wish we could have seen Michael trying to do comedy bits with like a birthing instructor.
真希望我们能看到迈克尔在产前辅导课上试图讲笑话的样子。

730
00:33:11.630 --> 00:33:13.430
I would have loved to seen that scene.
我真的很想看那场戏。

731
00:33:13.650 --> 00:33:16.730
I think what Jan has done to Michael is so cruel.
我觉得简对迈克尔所做的一切太残忍了。

732
00:33:16.730 --> 00:33:19.510
I know that she didn't call him.
我知道她没给他打电话。

733
00:33:19.510 --> 00:33:24.090
And also in that scene, Jan is like, Michael, you don't know what I have been through.
而且在那场戏里，简说，迈克尔，你根本不知道我经历了什么。

734
00:33:24.190 --> 00:33:26.410
And he said, no, no, I don't.
他说，不，不，我确实不知道。

735
00:33:26.710 --> 00:33:28.930
And I love Steve's delivery on that.
我特别喜欢史蒂夫在那里的演绎。

736
00:33:29.030 --> 00:33:29.430
I know.
我知道。

737
00:33:29.710 --> 00:33:33.470
I guess she feels bad and she lets him hold the baby, but it says the baby has to stay
我想她大概是觉得愧疚，就让他抱了抱宝宝，但要求宝宝必须待在

738
00:33:33.470 --> 00:33:34.250
in the car seat.
汽车安全座椅里。

739
00:33:34.610 --> 00:33:39.710
And then Michael has this very sweet talking head where he says he loves babies and he
然后迈克尔有一段非常暖心的采访，他说他喜欢宝宝，而且他

740
00:33:39.710 --> 00:33:41.770
tries to pick them up and hold one every day.
每天都会试着去抱抱他们。

741
00:33:41.950 --> 00:33:43.350
It just nourishes him.
这让他感到满足。

742
00:33:43.890 --> 00:33:48.930
And then we see this really sweet montage of Michael and babies and the babies love him.
接着我们看到了一段迈克尔和宝宝们在一起的温馨剪辑，宝宝们都很喜欢他。

743
00:33:48.930 --> 00:33:49.890
They really do.
他们确实很喜欢他。

744
00:33:50.250 --> 00:33:53.730
Well, that's because it's Steve Carell is holding the babies.
嗯，那是因为是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔在抱着宝宝们。

745
00:33:53.970 --> 00:33:58.050
I mean, not to say that they wouldn't have loved Michael, but Steve is a natural with
我是说，并不是说他们不会喜欢迈克尔，但史蒂夫确实很有

746
00:33:58.050 --> 00:33:58.390
kids.
孩子缘。

747
00:33:58.530 --> 00:33:58.930
I know.
我知道。

748
00:33:59.330 --> 00:34:01.230
We had a fan question from Evan L.
我们收到了来自埃文·L.

749
00:34:01.350 --> 00:34:02.390
and Stacey M.
和斯泰西·M.的粉丝提问。

750
00:34:02.590 --> 00:34:07.490
In the scenes where Michael is holding all the babies, were those hired actors or did the
在迈克尔抱着所有宝宝的那些戏份里，那些是请来的演员，还是

751
00:34:07.490 --> 00:34:11.390
crew just go out and let people line up to have their baby held by Steve Carell?
